  :notes "Tightens the wave45 --execute-dry-run audit so it explicitly drives the workstation_dispatch substrate instead of bridge mode.\n\nWhether Rust/MCP changed or why blueprint + checker were sufficient: only .missiond/v3/missiond-blueprint.lisp and scripts/check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs changed. The four Rust/MCP files in the write-scope (crates/missiond-daemon/src/handlers/knowledge/request.rs, .../unified_entry.rs, .../plan.rs, crates/missiond-mcp/src/tools/knowledge/request.rs) remain UNTOUCHED. Rationale: requirement #6 says only touch Rust/MCP if the live internal dry-run reveals a real forwarding/schema bug; it did not. Surveyed evidence on the running daemon: (1) request.rs::RespondDecision::ExecutePlan branch (line ~1169) forwards execute_mode/dispatch_strategy/dry_run/target/objective/cwd along with target_project/flow_id/scheduler_mode/parallelism/project/review_question_id when building pipeline_args for unified_entry::run_pipeline. (2) unified_entry::build_plan_execute_args (line ~501) forwards execute_mode/dispatch_strategy/dry_run/target/objective/cwd/target_project/requested_cwd verbatim to mission_plan execute. (3) plan.rs::action_execute_internal (line ~7331) builds InferenceContext from merged_hints and calls workstation_dispatch::evaluate_dispatch_decision; with target=mission_task_delegate + dispatch_strategy=agent-team (an INFERABLE_DISPATCH_STRATEGY) + non-empty objective + cwd as the requested_cwd scoping signal, the decision becomes Inferred/enabled, the substrate runs run_workstation_dispatch_with_contract_and_trace, and dry_run=true returns WorkstationDispatchOutcome::DryRun. build_workstation_dispatch_response then emits status=dry_run, execute_mode=internal, runner_status=workstation_dispatch_v0, target_tool=mission_task_delegate, dispatch_strategy=agent-team, with outcome_to_response_fields adding workstation_dispatch_status=dry_run_no_dispatch and task_brief_preview. (4) MCP schema's mission_request already exposes execute_mode (with the bridge|internal enum), dispatch_strategy, dry_run, target, objective, and cwd as explicit properties since wave43. Per requirement #6 and pattern-card lisp-first-before-checker: when blueprint + checker can pin the invariant, leave Rust/MCP alone.\n\nDefault live IPC behavior versus --execute-dry-run behavior:\n  - Default --live-ipc: 4 steps. start -> approve_intent -> approve_plan -> compat_write_audit. After approve_plan the smoke STOPS at review_packet.state=awaiting_execution; execute_plan is never called. live_ipc.execute_dry_run_requested=false. Wave44 compat_write_audit invariant still holds: new_alignment_subdirs=[] and new_plan_subdirs=[].\n  - --execute-dry-run: 5 steps. start -> approve_intent -> approve_plan -> execute_plan_dry_run -> compat_write_audit. After approve_plan the smoke calls mission_request action=respond response=execute_plan execute=true dry_run=true execute_mode=internal dispatch_strategy=agent-team cwd=<repo> target=mission_task_delegate objective=<smoke objective>. The execute_plan_dry_run step asserts the wave45 review-level invariants (respond_outcome=dispatched, inner_action='unified_entry::plan_execute', respond_result.execute=true, review_packet.state=execute_requested, review_packet.execute_allowed=true, allowed_responses=['observe'], request-local execute_plan event 000004.event.lisp appended whose body contains ':decision :execute_plan') AND the wave46 substrate-level invariants (pipeline_result.execute_mode='internal', status='dry_run', runner_status='workstation_dispatch_v0', workstation_dispatch_status='dry_run_no_dispatch', target_tool='mission_task_delegate', dispatch_strategy='agent-team', task_brief_preview is a non-empty string). The pipeline_result is hydrated from request.rs::tool_result_payload (which serde_json::from_str's the inner ToolResult text), so the smoke reads pipeline_result.* fields directly.\n\nThe exact internal no-dispatch proof observed in pipeline_result: against the daemon at HEAD, every --execute-dry-run run returned the workstation-dispatch substrate dry-run shape:\n  status='dry_run',\n  execute_mode='internal',\n  runner_status='workstation_dispatch_v0',\n  workstation_dispatch_status='dry_run_no_dispatch',\n  target_tool='mission_task_delegate',\n  dispatch_strategy='agent-team',\n  task_brief_preview present (non-empty string).\nThis is the build_workstation_dispatch_response branch with outcome=WorkstationDispatchOutcome::DryRun in plan.rs (line ~7993) plus outcome_to_response_fields (workstation_dispatch.rs line ~1751 + 1818). The smoke's no_dispatch_proof boolean now requires this exact shape; bridge mode (status=bridge_ready / runner_status=bridge_only) is no longer accepted as a no-dispatch proof for --execute-dry-run, so a future drift back to bridge would surface as a failure rather than passing silently. The blueprint's tightened (execute-dry-run-smoke ...) sub-form pins this single proof under :no-dispatch-proofs ((workstation-dispatch-substrate :status \"dry_run\" :execute_mode \"internal\" :runner_status \"workstation_dispatch_v0\" :workstation_dispatch_status \"dry_run_no_dispatch\" :target_tool \"mission_task_delegate\" :dispatch_strategy \"agent-team\" :task_brief_preview :present)).\n\nWhether a workstation slot or BoardTask was consumed by the smoke: NO workstation slot was consumed. The substrate returned WorkstationDispatchOutcome::DryRun, which builds the brief but does NOT call the inner mission_task_delegate handler, does NOT emit evidence, and does NOT spawn or claim any slot. Plan FSM is also untouched on the dry-run branch (plan.rs only transitions to Executing on Dispatched). DB rows: the live flow created the standard request-flow rows (a directive, an approved plan v2, and a hidden BoardTask anchor for the request) as audit records — those are kept by design (cleanup.kept_db_rows documents this explicitly) and do NOT correspond to a queued or dispatched workstation BoardTask. Filesystem-only: a request-local .missiond/requests/<request_id>/ directory with request.lisp, intent-alignment.lisp, plan.lisp (stamped with :plan_id/:version/:board_task_id), and events/000001..000004.event.lisp.\n\nWhether any request-local or compatibility artifacts were left behind after --cleanup:\n  - Request-local: nothing left. The cleanup block runs after all assertions pass and removes .missiond/requests/<request_id>/ in full (defensive prefix check). All three --cleanup acceptance runs (wave46-request-internal-dry-run-v0 + -exec + -json) report cleanup.removed_path equal to the request directory; ls .missiond/requests/ shows no wave46-* dirs after the run.\n  - Compatibility: nothing leaked. compat_write_audit reports new_alignment_subdirs=[] and new_plan_subdirs=[] for every acceptance run. The wave44 invariant (default flow does not pass write_file=true) is preserved unchanged in --execute-dry-run mode; the execute_plan respond path inherits the same args-derived compat_write_requested boolean from normalize_start_args's wave44 helper.\n  - Database: per pattern-card request-local-cleanup-stays-narrow, DB rows (directives, plans, board_tasks) created by the live flow remain as audit records. cleanup.kept_db_rows documents this explicitly.\n\nAggregate gate stays daemon-free and non-executing: scripts/check-v3-code-isomorphism-complete.mjs continues to spawn check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs with no flags; PER_SURFACE_CHECKERS does not include --execute-dry-run or --live-ipc. The aggregate run ('7 per-surface checkers passed') confirms this.\n\nLisp-first ordering preserved: blueprint changed first. The tightened (execute-dry-run-smoke ...) sub-form lives under unified-entry as a sibling of review-packet/review-response/tool-schema-contract/compat-writer-policy and now declares :rule (substrate-driven), :audit-flag :--execute-dry-run, :respond-args (:response :execute_plan :execute true :dry_run true :execute_mode :internal :dispatch_strategy :agent-team :target :mission_task_delegate), :asserts (the 13 assertions the JS smoke runs — 7 review-level + 6 substrate-level), :no-dispatch-proofs (a single workstation-dispatch-substrate proof shape pinning all six substrate fields plus task_brief_preview), :non-goal (default --live-ipc and aggregate gate stay non-executing), and :rationale (cite wave43/44/45 progress; this wave eliminates the bridge-mode loophole that bypassed the substrate)."
